course: dictionary
lesson: 11063
title: Weevils: tiny pests with long snouts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A weevil is a small beetle with a long snout, which is the long front part of its head with the mouth at the tip. Weevils eat and damage crops, flour, rice, grain and nuts. «Weevils are beetles with a long snout with tiny jaws at the tip, used to drill holes in nuts and seeds for their eggs.»
explain: Use the context to work out what a word means. Words like «damages» and «spoil» tell you a weevil is harmful, not friendly. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Pests can be spotted by the damage they cause. «The boll weevil ate so much cotton that farmers grew other crops» shows that a pest can change what people grow and eat. Swap in your meaning: a weevil is a small beetle that spoils crops. Does it still make sense? Yes, so you have it right.
fact: A weevil is a small beetle with a long snout.
fact: Weevils eat and damage crops, flour, rice, grain and nuts.
fact: «The boll weevil ate so much cotton that farmers grew other crops» in Alabama, and the town of Enterprise built a statue to it.
fact: «Weevils in the flour» means the flour is spoiled, so it is thrown out.
fact: There are tens of thousands of kinds of weevil, so they are one of the biggest beetle families.
exercise: What is a weevil? | A small fish with a long tail | *A small beetle with a long snout | A kind of flour sold in shops
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the long part at the front of the weevil's head. | *snout | jaws | tip | beetles
exercise: Why would you throw out flour with weevils in it? | *It has been spoiled by pests | It is now too sweet | It has gone too white
test: The giraffe weevil is found only in Madagascar. What does «only» tell you? | *It is found in one place | It lives in the sea | It has no home at all | It is found everywhere on Earth
test: «Rice and grain weevils lay eggs inside grains, where the grubs grow.» Where do the grubs grow? | *Inside grains | In the sea | On the roof of the barn | In the sky
exam: What kind of animal is a weevil? | A fish | *A beetle | A bird | A snake
